{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261111T192148Z-3405d669", "ts": "2026-11-11T19:24:53Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev", "branch": "feature/ci-testament", "build": "6a4f5166edbc"}, "body": {"base_commit": "6a4f5166edbcc2823b00467a8eea4dd9280863c7", "base_tree": "060e018ba551b6eb1e6c730a547ac57032e22c9b", "head_tree": "def7d798da5e15814698a6845bb2a994a0fff4ca", "head_commit": "0c4a1c1c4fb731a411ca342ea0fe52760b9f625d", "dispatch_commit": "0c4a1c1c4fb731a411ca342ea0fe52760b9f625d", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "rule-2 cumulative: branch is 2 commits ahead of origin/develop, working tree clean, no fresh cumulative-mode record for current HEAD, and no composed review coverage spans the branch", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", ".testament.toml", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md", "pyproject.toml", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_changed": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", ".testament.toml", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md", "pyproject.toml", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The key is kept out of a test process's environment, but the test process can still read it from its parent's /proc/<ppid>/environ", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: `suite_env` filters only the env a child is handed, but on Linux `/proc/<pid>/environ` holds a process's initial environment and is readable by any process with the same uid. `tools/ci-suite.py` starts with TESTAMENT_KEY in its environ, and so does the step's bash. So every pytest it launches can read the key. That covers the selected-out run after a pool verdict and the whole-suite run on every keyed fallback, and with them every unpinned dev-extra dependency that pytest imports. The plan's constraint says the key reaches 'never a test process'. `suite_env`'s docstring says 'The key must never reach a test process'. The workflow already keeps the key off the dependency-install step against exactly this kind of supply-chain code, but that protection does not reach the place it is meant for (core learning: 'When defense-in-depth is the reason a risk needn't be verified, check the defense is REACHABLE from the failure'). `test_pytest_on_the_job_sees_nothing_of_testaments` checks only the weaker property, the env mapping passed to subprocess.run. There are two fixes. (a) Split the step: a keyed step runs only the fetch, install and pool run, and writes its verdict and decision (pool verdict, fallback or refusal) to a file or `$GITHUB_OUTPUT`. A following step with no key runs pytest on the job and combines the results. Then pin with the conventions test that the pytest-running step's env carries no secret. (b) Accept the exposure as a recorded decision and narrow the docstring, the change record and the plan constraint to what holds: the key is not in a test process's environment.", "files": ["tools/ci-suite.py", ".github/workflows/tests.yml", "tests/test_ci_suite.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Annotation title escaping is untested, and every failing pytest id needs it", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `_describe` passes each failing item's id (`tests/x.py::test_y`) as an `::error title=...::` property. Workflow-command property values must have ':' and ',' encoded, which is the `property_value=True` branch of `_escape`. No test reaches that branch. `test_a_message_cannot_end_its_own_command_or_start_another` covers the message encoding only, and `test_the_summary_names_the_failing_test_and_no_runner` matches the id in the summary lines, not the annotation. If the property branch were deleted or broken, every failing-test annotation would be malformed and the suite would stay green. Add an assertion on the exact annotation line for FAILED, e.g. `::error title=tests/test_a.py%3A%3Atest_b::assert 1 == 2`, and confirm it goes red with the property encoding removed.", "files": ["tools/ci-suite.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py"], "fid": "R-2"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 2, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The 30-minute job limit is described as room for the worst path, but nothing has measured it", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The worst path the comment names adds up to: two pool waits of up to 600 s each (20 min), plus the console download (per-operation timeout 120 s), the venv and wheel install, and the whole suite on a 4-core runner with 5 workers, all after checkout and the dependency install. The old limit for the suite alone was 20 minutes, and no CI timing is recorded. If the job-side suite takes more than about 7 minutes, this path is cut off with no verdict, which is the outcome POOL_WAIT_SECONDS says it exists to prevent. Read the job-side suite duration from the branch's first CI run that falls back, and set the limit, or POOL_WAIT_SECONDS, from that figure.", "files": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "A rate-limited console (429/408) is classed as a refusal and fails the job with key-replacement guidance", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `fetch_cli` treats any HTTP status below 500 as Refused. A transient 429 or 408 from a busy console therefore turns CI red with 'this job cannot use the pool'. running-tests.md then points the reader at the key ('A replaced key is the usual cause'), although nothing about the key is wrong. Classify 408 and 429 as Unavailable, as the runner's own principle requires ('Anything not known to be an outage is a refusal' \u2014 these are known to be one), and add them to the outage parametrization.", "files": ["tools/ci-suite.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py"], "oid": "O-2"}], "duration_seconds": 660, "scope": "ci-testament", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": "6a4f5166edbcc2823b00467a8eea4dd9280863c7", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-11T19:21:55Z"}}

